{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/239441-on-merits-and-conditions-in-pacts","id":239441,"title":"On Merits and Conditions in Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-24T12:30:16-07:00","id":239441,"title":"On Merits and Conditions in Pacts","content":"If a negative Condition is repaired as part of a Pact, how does it function in the Pact Aspect equation? Is it absorbed as part of the Cover benefit for the demon, or can it just be 'smoothed over'?<br /> <br /> Also, if a demon wants an aspect of a mortal's life represented by a Merit as part of her Cover, do the Merit benefits just switch over with the Cover aspect (switching the Merit between character sheets, as it were), or is it just the appearance of the Merit, forcing the demon to rely on Legend? And if the latter, what happens to the mortal's Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T16:13:38-07:00","id":256346,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you mean with the first question. Can you elaborate?<br /> <br /> As to your second question: I would say the person losing the Merit loses it completely and probably uses the dots to buy whatever they gain from the Pact (or just gets the dots back via Sanctity of Merits). The Demon would have to buy the Merit with experience or rely on Legend.Of course, I would probably let this sort of Merit buy be done with Cover Experience or normal Experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T17:06:43-07:00","id":256365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what you mean with the first question. Can you elaborate? </div> </div> </div>Say a character has a 'Bad Eyesight' Condition. If she enters into a Pact to repair it, is her astigmatism actually fixed, or is it just turned into a nascent element that the demon can later use in a Cover (in mechanical terms, a Cover Experience)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T21:39:50-07:00","id":256469,"title":"","content":"I suppose the ailment would be fixed; but if the Pact were somehow broken/destroyed (assuming it was permanent in the first place) it would probably come back (and the Demon would lose it, and have to roll for Compromise as part of her Cover suddenly starts to deteriorate and the Cover tries to quantumly compensate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}